From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 20:47:28 +0200
Subject: ARM: dts: allwinner: sun8i-a83t: Use the non-secure SCPI channels

Crust reserves msgbox channels 0/1 and the top two 256 B slots of SRAM
A2 for the secure SCPI client, and channels 2/3 with the slots below
for the non-secure one. The A83T kernel now boots through a PSCI
monitor that is the secure client, so Linux has to be on 2/3 with the
shared memory at 0x13c00, exactly like H3/H5 (and as this node was
originally written before the kernel became the secure client itself).

Also fix the unit address vs reg mismatch this reintroduces
(scp-shmem@13c00 was pointing at 0x13e00) and the space indentation
on the syscon node.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-a83t.dtsi | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-a83t.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-a83t.dtsi
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-a83t.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/sun8i-a83t.dtsi
@@ -292,7 +292,7 @@ opp-1800000000 {
 
 	scpi_protocol: scpi {
 		compatible = "arm,scpi";
-		mboxes = <&msgbox 0>, <&msgbox 1>;
+		mboxes = <&msgbox 2>, <&msgbox 3>;
 		mbox-names = "tx", "rx";
 		shmem = <&scpi_sram>;
 	};
@@ -430,9 +430,9 @@ syscon: syscon@1c00000 {
 			compatible = "allwinner,sun8i-a83t-system-controller",
 				"syscon";
 			reg = <0x01c00000 0x1000>;
-                        #address-cells = <1>;
-                        #size-cells = <1>;
-                        ranges;
+			#address-cells = <1>;
+			#size-cells = <1>;
+			ranges;
 
 			sram_a2: sram@40000 {
 				compatible = "mmio-sram";
@@ -443,7 +443,7 @@ sram_a2: sram@40000 {
 
 				scpi_sram: scp-shmem@13c00 {
 					compatible = "arm,scp-shmem";
-					reg = <0x13e00 0x200>;
+					reg = <0x13c00 0x200>;
 				};
 			};
 
